html_doc=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="n8n Node Atlas: engineering documentation, real-world examples, and searchable core node reference."><title>n8n Node Atlas · Engineering Docs</title><style>{css}</style></head><body><div class="app"><header class="topbar"><button class="menu-btn" id="menu" aria-label="Open navigation">☰</button><a class="brand" href="#docs"><span class="brand-mark">n8n</span><span>Node Atlas</span></a><nav class="top-tabs" aria-label="Primary"><button class="tab-btn active" data-tab="docs">Documentation</button><button class="tab-btn" data-tab="examples">Working examples <sup>50</sup></button></nav><span class="top-spacer"></span><button class="mode-btn" id="mode" title="Toggle color mode">◐ <span id="mode-label">System</span></button></header><div class="layout"><aside class="sidebar" id="sidebar"><div class="side-title">Documentation</div><a class="tree-link" href="#overview">Overview</a><a class="tree-link" href="#architecture">Architecture</a><a class="tree-link" href="#data">Data & expressions</a><a class="tree-link" href="#reliability">Reliability & security</a><a class="tree-link" href="#recipes">Pattern recipes</a><div class="side-title">Node reference</div>{cat_nav}<div class="side-title">Dedicated tab</div><a class="tree-link" href="#examples" data-open-tab="examples">50 working examples <span>↗</span></a><div class="side-title">External</div><a class="tree-link" href="https://docs.n8n.io/" target="_blank">Official n8n docs ↗</a></aside><main class="content"><div class="panel active" id="docs"><section class="hero" id="overview"><div><span class="kicker">Engineering documentation · core package {esc(version)}</span><h1>Build workflows that hold up in production.</h1><p>A documentation system for n8n nodes, workflow architecture, failure handling, data contracts, and practical automation design. Search the core node atlas or switch to 50 end-to-end working examples.</p><div class="hero-actions"><button class="primary" data-tab="examples">Browse working examples</button><a class="secondary" href="#catalog">Explore node reference</a></div></div>{hero_visual}</section><section class="section" id="architecture"><span class="kicker">01 · Architecture</span><h2>Think in boundaries, not boxes.</h2><p class="section-intro">A reliable workflow separates ingress, normalization, decisioning, side effects, and operations. The visual language below uses n8n-editor-style node cards, connectors, labels, and a grid canvas rather than generic architecture rectangles.</p><div class="cards"><article class="feature"><span class="kicker">Ingress</span><h3>Triggers establish contracts</h3><p>Document event shape, authentication, replay behavior, response timing, and the correlation ID before adding business logic.</p></article><article class="feature"><span class="kicker">Execution</span><h3>Items are the unit of work</h3><p>Normalize types at boundaries, preserve stable identifiers, and avoid hidden dependencies on item position or branch ordering.</p></article><article class="feature"><span class="kicker">Operations</span><h3>Side effects need safeguards</h3><p>Use credentials, timeouts, bounded retries, idempotency keys, and an explicit error workflow around every fallible integration.</p></article></div></section><section class="section" id="data"><span class="kicker">02 · Data model</span><h2>Make data contracts explicit.</h2><div class="doc-list"><article class="feature"><h3>Expressions first</h3><div class="code">{{ $json.customer.email }}
{{ $json.items.map(item => item.sku) }}
{{ $now.toISO() }}
{{ $('Normalize').item.json.customerId }}</div><p>Use expressions for local mapping. Choose Code only for genuine multi-item aggregation, libraries, or stateful logic.</p></article><article class="feature"><h3>Boundary checklist</h3><ul><li>Required fields and types are explicit.</li><li>Null, empty, and missing are distinct.</li><li>Dates have an agreed timezone.</li><li>Remote failures are classified.</li><li>Binary size and retention are bounded.</li><li>External IDs are retained for replay.</li></ul></article></div></section><section class="section" id="reliability"><span class="kicker">03 · Reliability & security</span><h2>Design for retries and failure.</h2><div class="callout"><b>Production gate:</b> validate credentials, error paths, retry policy, rate-limit behavior, duplicate delivery, and partial failure before publishing a workflow.</div><div class="doc-list"><article class="feature"><h3>Idempotency</h3><p>Derive a deterministic key from provider event ID and operation. Check it before a write, then persist the result with the key.</p></article><article class="feature"><h3>Dead letters</h3><p>Capture execution ID, node, correlation ID, sanitized input summary, and retry classification. Never put secrets in alerts.</p></article><article class="feature"><h3>Security boundaries</h3><p>Keep tokens in n8n credentials, minimize PII, validate signatures before parsing, and treat all remote data as untrusted.</p></article><article class="feature"><h3>Observability</h3><p>Carry correlation IDs and record outcome, duration, provider status, item counts, and the workflow version.</p></article></div></section><section class="section" id="recipes"><span class="kicker">04 · Patterns</span><h2>Reusable workflow recipes.</h2><div class="cards"><article class="feature"><h3>Paginated ingestion</h3><p>Follow a provider cursor, cap pages, upsert by natural key, and persist the cursor only after a successful page.</p></article><article class="feature"><h3>Human approval</h3><p>Persist pending state, authenticate the callback, validate current state, and make approve/reject idempotent.</p></article><article class="feature"><h3>Stateless sub-workflow</h3><p>Define inputs and outputs as a versioned contract. Extract for reuse, isolation, testing, or an agent tool—not just canvas tidiness.</p></article></div></section><section class="section" id="catalog"><span class="kicker">05 · Reference</span><h2>Official core node catalog.</h2><p class="section-intro">Generated from the official <code>n8n-nodes-base</code> package manifest. Use the live n8n schema for exact operation-specific parameters and conditional fields.</p><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><strong>{len(nodes)}</strong><span>core node entries</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{len(cats)}</strong><span>responsibility families</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>50</strong><span>working examples</span></div></div><div class="catalog-toolbar"><input class="search" id="node-search" placeholder="Search nodes, IDs, or source paths…" aria-label="Search nodes"></div>{cat_sections}</section><div class="footer">Generated from <code>n8n-nodes-base@{esc(version)}</code>. Core package coverage is pinned at build time; community nodes and version-specific parameters are not silently labeled complete. · <a href="https://docs.n8n.io/" target="_blank">Official n8n documentation ↗</a></div></div><div class="panel" id="examples"><section class="section" style="margin-top:10px"><span class="kicker">Dedicated examples tab</span><h1>50 working automation blueprints.</h1><p class="section-intro">Each example is a concrete end-to-end use case with a node sequence, implementation guidance, and production checklist. Open the corresponding workflow in n8n, configure credentials, then validate against your instance’s live node schema.</p><div class="examples-toolbar"><input class="search" id="example-search" placeholder="Search the 50 examples…" aria-label="Search examples"></div><div class="example-grid">{examples_cards}</div></section><div class="footer">Examples are implementation blueprints, not pre-authenticated workflows. Credentials remain in your n8n instance.</div></div></main></div></div><script>
const root=document.documentElement;const stored=localStorage.getItem('atlas-theme')||'system';let mode=stored;function applyMode(){{root.dataset.theme=mode==='system'?(matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches?'dark':'light'):mode;document.querySelector('#mode-label').textContent=mode[0].toUpperCase()+mode.slice(1)}}applyMode();document.querySelector('#mode').addEventListener('click',()=>{{mode=mode==='system'?'light':mode==='light'?'dark':'system';localStorage.setItem('atlas-theme',mode);applyMode()}});const sidebar=document.querySelector('#sidebar');document.querySelector('#menu').addEventListener('click',()=>sidebar.classList.toggle('open'));function showTab(name){{document.querySelectorAll('.panel').forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle('active',x.id===name));document.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn').forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle('active',x.dataset.tab===name));sidebar.classList.remove('open');window.scrollTo({{top:0,behavior:'smooth'}})}}document.querySelectorAll('[data-tab]').forEach(x=>x.addEventListener('click',()=>showTab(x.dataset.tab)));document.querySelectorAll('[data-open-tab]').forEach(x=>x.addEventListener('click',e=>{{e.preventDefault();showTab('examples')}}));function wireSearch(input,selector){{const el=document.querySelector(input);if(!el)return;const cards=[...document.querySelectorAll(selector)];el.addEventListener('input',()=>{{const q=el.value.toLowerCase();cards.forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle('hidden',q&&!x.dataset.search.includes(q)))}})}}wireSearch('#node-search','.node-reference');wireSearch('#example-search','.example-card');</script></body></html>'''
(OUT/'index.html').write_text(html_doc)
(OUT/'.nojekyll').write_text('')
(ROOT/'README.md').write_text(f'''# n8n Node Atlas\n\nDetailed static documentation for n8n core nodes, engineering patterns, and 50 real-world workflow blueprints.\n\n- Official package: `n8n-nodes-base@{version}`\n- Core node entries: {len(nodes)}\n- Working examples: 50\n- Responsive desktop/mobile docs shell\n- Hierarchy-driven sidebar\n- Documentation / Working examples tabs\n- Editor-style n8n node visuals\n- Light / dark / system mode toggle\n\n## Scope\n\nThe node catalog is generated from the official core package manifest at build time. Community nodes and version-specific operation parameters are not represented as core coverage.\n''')
print({'package_version':version,'nodes':len(nodes),'examples':len(examples),'html_bytes':(OUT/'index.html').stat().st_size})
